Q1. What is the Strategy Design Pattern?
Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

The Strategy Pattern is a
Behavioral Design Pattern
that defines a family of
interchangeable algorithms
and allows the client to
select one algorithm at runtime.

Each algorithm is encapsulated
inside its own class.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need Strategy Pattern?

• Select algorithms at runtime.
• Remove long if-else/switch statements.
• Reduce Tight Coupling.
• Improve Maintainability.
• Improve Extensibility.
• Follow Open/Closed Principle.

------------------------------------------------------------

What problem does it solve?

Without Strategy,

multiple algorithms are written
inside one class using
if-else or switch statements.

As new algorithms are added,

the code becomes difficult
to maintain.

Strategy separates each
algorithm into its own class.

------------------------------------------------------------

