Q2. How does Strategy Pattern
remove if-else statements?

Interview Ready Answer

Without Strategy Pattern

Payment

↓

if(UPI)

↓

UPI Logic

else if(Card)

↓

Card Logic

else if(Net Banking)

↓

Net Banking Logic

Problems

• Tight Coupling.
• Difficult to Maintain.
• Difficult to Extend.
• Every new payment method
  requires modifying
  existing code.

------------------------------------------------------------

With Strategy Pattern

Payment Context

↓

PaymentStrategy

        ▲
        │
 ┌──────┼───────────┐
 │      │           │
UPI   Card   Net Banking

↓

Client selects one strategy

↓

pay()

Each payment method is
implemented separately.

The Payment Context delegates
the request to the selected strategy.

------------------------------------------------------------

Benefits

• Removes if-else/switch.
• Loose Coupling.
• Easy to add new algorithms.
• Better Readability.
• Better Maintainability.
• Better Scalability.

